  "findings": [
    "Actual bottom HardwareButtonsConstants and matching GPIO dictionary used; misleading inline comments ignored.",
    "Base LCD DC56/RST57 conflicts with current52/51 configuration; base PRESS52 would ground current LCD DC output when pressed.",
    "lcdpwm LCD matches current image but five button semantics differ: DOWN, RIGHT, PRESS, KEY1, KEY2.",
    "Both old LCD drivers use SPI0.0 at40MHz with no backlight GPIO; reviewed image override uses10MHz.",
    "Base KEY2/KEY3 useUART2 pins43/42; require GPIO pinmux and no UART2 owner.",
    "Only current FOX22 uses1.8V GPIO4_C0/C1 for buttons; switch-to-ground and correct-domain internal pulls are appropriate,3.3V pulls are not.",
    "Pinned button opener may retry without pull_up after EINVAL/EBUSY; verify released/pressed readings and effective pulls on target.",
    "Prior board installed button source unavailable in local cache; actual connected wiring remains unverified."
